   - **`Sources/ReachyMedia/CameraSession.swift`** — gained `public let dataChannel = WebRTCDataChannel()` (created at construction so it survives self-healing peer-connection restarts), `adopt(_:)` guarding `channel.label == "data"`, `dataChannel.detach()` in `teardownPeer()`, and `peerConnection(_:didOpen:)` is no longer a no-op.

   - **`Sources/ReachyMedia/RemoteRobotLink.swift`** (committed `60bbe8d`) — `@MainActor final class` assembling `CentralSignalingTransport` → `CameraSession` → `dataChannel` → `RemoteRobotConnection`. Camera comes free; 3D scene does not (URDF/STL are HTTP-only).

   - **`Sources/ReachyKit/Session/RobotSession.swift` / `RobotSession+Connect.swift`** (committed `60bbe8d`) — the whole connection protocol moved into the sibling file for length. `makeClient` became internal. New:
     ```swift
     @discardableResult
     func connect(using client: any RobotAPIClient) async -> Bool {
         automaticConnectionAllowed = true
         let attemptID = beginAttempt(at: nil)
         return await settle(client: client, address: nil, attemptID: attemptID, automatically: false)
